  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1222 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nImpacts in temperatures from the front will not be felt until after \nthe weekend as the front pushes through the rest of the region on \nMonday. Short wave ridging aloft will build overhead Monday and \nTuesday. However, easterly upslope flow will keep temperatures much \ncloser and even below seasonal averages through much of the week. \nUpslope flow will promote periodic convective chances Monday lasting \nthrough the week. Increasing southwest flow aloft starting around \nmid-week will keep convective chances going through the remainder of \nthe week. Low level flow returning to the south will start to bring \ntemperatures back up in the second half of the week.",
